  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.8.2`\n\n### Features\n\n- collapse tabs out of the tab bar and reopen them later: a tab's context menu and a title-bar list put tabs away in sets that survive restarts, each terminal's content is kept in collapsed-scrollback/ and shown again on reopen, and secrets are dropped from the stored tabs as they are for the session; a set reopens at the end of the bar with only the first tab connecting at once, and collapsing skips the reopen-closed-tab history so a tab can't come back twice ([748c8789](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/748c878948e4ef2a7460d139b0f6411e2c8afe53))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.8.2...v0.8.3-beta.1](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.8.2...v0.8.3-beta.1)",
